## Pin: B12 — `unsafe include Send` is the explicit-safety-assertion
## variant; behaves like a plain `include Send` for v1 (no
## auto-derive to suppress), so a class containing a raw pointer
## still typechecks through Mutex.new / Thread.spawn.
##
## NOTE: spec example writes `include unsafe Send` but the parser
## accepts the `unsafe include Send` token order (consistent with
## Ruby's `private def …` modifier style). This is a known
## spec-vs-grammar wording mismatch; the SEMANTICS match.
## See docs/specs/ownership/send_sync_enforcement.spec.md §B12.

class WrapsRawPointer
  unsafe include Send

  def init
  end
end

def main
  let w = WrapsRawPointer.new
  let _m = Mutex.new(w)
end
